Hey @anangl, I actually have a board with three normal polarity PWM channels on PWM0 that broke after this. :-)

Seems like the problem is related to the polarity, if you change this on an nrf52dk:

```patch
diff --git a/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832-pinctrl.dtsi b/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832-pinctrl.dtsi
index c859969e55..d2a3ec8b5d 100644
--- a/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832-pinctrl.dtsi
+++ b/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832-pinctrl.dtsi
@@ -56,7 +56,6 @@
        pwm0_default: pwm0_default {
                group1 {
                        psels = <NRF_PSEL(PWM_OUT0, 0, 17)>;
-                       nordic,invert;
                };
        };
 
diff --git a/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832.dts b/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832.dts
index dd72d7d62f..3e7e58735a 100644
--- a/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832.dts
+++ b/boards/arm/nrf52dk_nrf52832/nrf52dk_nrf52832.dts
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
        pwmleds {
                compatible = "pwm-leds";
                pwm_led0: pwm_led_0 {
-                       pwms = <&pwm0 0 PWM_MSEC(20) PWM_POLARITY_INVERTED>;
+                       pwms = <&pwm0 0 PWM_MSEC(20) PWM_POLARITY_NORMAL>;
                };
        };
````

And then run `samples/basic/fade_led`, the led does not fade. It works alright with the inverted polarity and by rolling back this patch. Could you look into it?

issue_context.body:
I have a custom NRF52840 board with 8 LED's and I use pwm API led_on(), led_off, led_blink() etc, to turn them on, set brightness and blink and everything works fine except one case
When I have more than 1 LED's blinking I cannot turn them off
The reason is this block of code in SDK\zephyr\drivers\pwm\pwm_nrfx.c, function  pwm_period_check_and_set()

```c
/* If any other channel (other than the one being configured) is set up
     * with a non-zero pulse cycle, the period that is currently set cannot
     * be changed, as this would influence the output for this channel.
     */
    for (i = 0; i < NRF_PWM_CHANNEL_COUNT; ++i) {
        if (i != channel) {
            uint16_t channel_pulse_cycle =
                data->current[i]
                & PWM_NRFX_CH_PULSE_CYCLES_MASK;
            if (channel_pulse_cycle > 0) {
                LOG_ERR("Incompatible period.");
                return -EINVAL;
            }
        }
    }
```
When multiple LED's are blinking the expression evaluates to true and the code returns -EINVAL and the LED's are not turned off
If I comment out that code block I can turn off multiple blinking LED's 
It seems that the code should detect the case where LED's are be turned off i.e their brightness is set to zero and allow that
